--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,51 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Account settings and passkey service
+
+Account settings live at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Password sign-in stores the
+service's `token` in tab-scoped session storage and opens settings. Tokens are sent as
+`Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the service must validate them and enforce account
+ownership for every request. A 401 clears the local session. No credentials are seeded
+or stored in the frontend.
+
+The existing remote service does not currently expose the passkey management endpoint
+(its `GET /passkeys` returns 404). To enable management, implement the contract below
+on that service, or set `PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_API_URL` at build time to an account API base
+URL. It must support CORS for the site's origin, Authorization and Content-Type headers,
+and GET, PATCH, DELETE and POST methods.
+
+- `POST /login` takes `{ "username": "…", "password": "…" }` and returns `{ "token": "…" }`.
+- `GET /passkeys` returns the complete, unpaginated list for the authenticated user:
+
+  ```json
+  {
+    "rpId": "your-site.example",
+    "user": { "id": "base64url-user-handle", "name": "reader@example.com", "displayName": "Reader" },
+    "passkeys": [
+      { "id": "base64url-credential-id", "displayName": "Personal laptop", "createdAt": "2026-10-01T12:00:00Z", "lastUsedAt": null }
+    ]
+  }
+  ```
+
+- `PATCH /passkeys/:id` takes `{ "displayName": "Personal laptop" }` and returns a 2xx
+  after persisting the label. Validate a trimmed name of 1–64 characters on the server.
+- `DELETE /passkeys/:id` returns a 2xx only after revoking the credential for sign-in.
+- Mutations must enforce ownership; unauthenticated requests return 401. The service
+  must never return another user's passkeys. Dates are optional ISO 8601 strings.
+
+`rpId` must be the original WebAuthn relying party ID, valid for the deployed origin.
+User handles and credential IDs are original, unpadded Base64URL values, not usernames
+or database row IDs. A partial list is unsafe: the browser may hide omitted credentials.
+
+After reading the authoritative list, the UI feature-detects WebAuthn Signal API methods
+and reports accepted credentials and current account identity. After confirmed removal
+it also reports the removed credential. Signal failures do not undo successful account
+changes; readers can retry with **Refresh & sync**. Passkey labels are site-specific:
+`signalCurrentUserDetails` reports the server's account identity, not individual key
+labels. Browser signals are advisory and password managers control their application.
+See the [WebAuthn Signal API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api).
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
